# Raw and intermediate data stay out of git: every one of them is reproducible from the code
# in src/ plus the source documentation in docs/sources/. data/out/ IS committed, because the
# harmonized store is the deliverable.
data/raw/
data/interim/
data/verify/
# data/out/ is the PRE-redaction internal store. It was committed to this public repository and
# leaked 24 personal email addresses, because redaction only ran when building the site payload.
# The published artifacts are site/data/, which pass src/redact.py. Headline figures are
# recorded in docs/00-state.md instead.
data/out/
# data/manual/ IS committed: it is curated input that cannot be regenerated from code.
!data/manual/
# data/frozen/ IS committed: the gzipped inputs the pipeline reads, about 8 MB, so a fresh
# clone can rebuild the published map without the 336 MB of original downloads.
# Built by python src/freeze.py.
!data/frozen/

# site/vendor/ and site/fonts/ ARE committed on purpose. The published page must make zero
# third-party requests apart from map tiles, so MapLibre and the two typefaces are served from
# the same origin and the deployment stays a plain static copy of site/.

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Never
.env
*.local.*
secrets/
